  "missingStatements": [
    {
      "text": "Trans women should be admitted to women's shelters, rape crisis centres and other women's services on the same terms as other women.",
      "value": 2,
      "rationale": "The Manifesto calls for shelters and crisis centres to serve trans women and for transfeminists to help them screen and train staff.",
      "sources": [
        "s1"
      ],
      "addedAs": "exclude-trans-women-women-only-spaces"
    },
    {
      "text": "Surgery on intersex children to make their bodies fit male or female should not be done without their own consent.",
      "value": 2,
      "rationale": "The Manifesto calls genital surgery on intersex children without consent inherently abusive and demands that people decide about their own bodies.",
      "sources": [
        "s1"
      ],
      "addedAs": "parents-choose-intersex-surgery"
    },
    {
      "text": "Being transgender should not be classified as a mental disorder, while medical treatment for transition stays available.",
      "value": 2,
      "rationale": "The Manifesto insists transsexuality is part of ordinary human variety and that depathologisation is compatible with making treatment more accessible; Serano's writing opposes pathologising diagnoses.",
      "sources": [
        "s1",
        "s12"
      ],
      "addedAs": "gender-identity-recognition"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sex workers' rights are workers' rights, and sex work should be treated as labour rather than as slavery.",
      "value": 2,
      "rationale": "Koyama's pamphlet argues prostitution is a type of work, not slavery, and that the movement is part of the labour movement.",
      "sources": [
        "s2"
      ],
      "addedAs": "legalize-sex-work"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Searched theme by theme: Koyama's Manifesto, her readings (sex work, harm reduction, shelters, race, abortion) and FAQ; Serano's website, blog and the Ms. essay; Stone; the Raha/van der Drift publisher text and Raha's abstract. The texts are rich on gender, bodies, medicine, violence, sexuality, intersectionality and trans inclusion, and nearly silent on economics, government, world affairs, technology and ecology, so those stay null. Koyama's own postscript says the Manifesto is narrow and focused on trans women. The old audit's economic, institutional and foreign-policy answers rested on the 'left outlook' and are dropped. Strands: Koyama treats sex and gender as constructed, Serano holds a holistic view with biology; Raha and van der Drift (abolitionist, anti-capitalist) go beyond the earlier mainstream. Raha's and van der Drift's book text, Serano's Whipping Girl and Excluded full text, Serano's Medium essays, Bettcher's Philosophy Compass article, Spade's and Feinberg's writings were not used (see report); Feinberg and Spade were left out as trans liberation rather than transfeminism.",
